Five minutes ago, there was heavy rain here.
Now it is not raining.
I go for a slow walk.
On the way, there is a Sunday market.
There is a lot of bustle here.
I stand in front of a fruit stall.
In front of me are these local mangoes.
At the back of the shop are those big mangoes.
I ask the shopkeeper, "Sir, what is the price of these local fruits?"
He says, "Madam, these fruits are very sweet."
"Their price is one hundred rupees."
I ask, "What is that?"
"What are those big fruits?"
The shopkeeper says, "Those come from another state."
"But these are the best."
Five months ago, I did not know these Indian fruits.
I think, I will buy these local fruits only.
I say, "Sir, please give these local fruits."
I give a hundred rupees to him.
The shopkeeper puts those fruits in a bag.
He gives the bag to me.
I take the bag, and go forward slowly.
